  "reason": "Evidence: The best config so far is config_001 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.725 acc. All 6 completed experiments use multiprofile; the singleprofile dimension is entirely unexplored. scvi_n200 is clearly the best RNA encoder (0.725 vs 0.520 for scgpt), imagenet_vit_l slightly outperforms resnet50 (0.725 vs 0.713), and weighted fusion edges out concat (0.725 vs 0.721). Question: Does singleprofile with the best-known encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l) and weighted fusion compete with or exceed the multiprofile+transformer pipeline? This is the largest unexplored architectural axis. Why this experiment: With only 3 experiments remaining, testing the singleprofile variant with the strongest component choices (config_046) reduces the most critical uncertainty. If it matches or beats 0.725, it opens a new exploitation direction; if it falls well short, we can confidently focus remaining budget on refining the multiprofile+transformer+weighted configuration. No other untested config addresses an equally important unknown with equally strong component choices."
